        "text": "All requested Python files have been successfully created in the current working directory. Here are the files and their purposes:\n\n1. **[SAME-SCENARIO] extract_text.py** - Extracts plain text from a scanned document image using Google Cloud Vision API.\n2. **[SAME-SCENARIO] extract_layout.py** - Extracts blocks, lines, tables, or layout elements from a document using Google Cloud Vision API.\n3. **[SAME-SCENARIO] extract_tables.py** - Extracts table cells and row structure from a document using Google Cloud Vision API.\n4. **[SAME-SCENARIO] extract_key_values.py** - Extracts key-value pairs from a form-like document using Google Cloud Vision API.\n5. **[HELPER] document_client.py** - Provides local configuration and client helper utilities for OCR and Layout Extraction using Google Cloud Vision API.\n6. **[HELPER] document_models.py** - Defines local request, response, and normalization helpers for OCR and Layout Extraction using Google Cloud Vision API.\n7. **[LATER-STEP] ocr_translate.py** - Translates extracted OCR text using Google Cloud Translation API.\n8. **[LATER-STEP] ocr_safety.py** - Checks extracted document text for unsafe content using regular expressions.\n9. **[LATER-STEP] document_field_extraction.py** - Extracts structured fields from OCR-normalized document text using regular expressions.\n10. **[LATER-STEP] ocr_embedding.py** - Embeds extracted document sections for semantic retrieval using the Sentence Transformers library.\n\nEach scored implementation file uses a concrete external provider and is identifiable in the code. The local helper files contain configuration loading, payload normalization, or response parsing utilities when useful.",
